  "worked_solution": "To evaluate the minor of ${a}_{11},$ we remove the first row and first column:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & \u2217 & \u2217 \\\\ \u2217 & p & 7 \\\\ \u2217 & -8 & p-15\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}p & 7 \\\\ -8 & p-15\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}p & 7 \\\\ -8 & p-15\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =p(p-15)-7(-8) \\\\  & ={p}^{2}-15p+56.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is $0$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{2}-15p+56 & =0 \\\\ (p-7)(p-8) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $p=7$ and $p=8.$",
